  "id": "rational-learning",
  "term": "rational learning",
  "definition": "Rational learning is a pattern of learning that appears statistically sensible, such as using the amount of prior evidence to decide how broadly or narrowly to generalize a word or category. In the source, this kind of behavior does not necessarily require explicit global statistical inference, because similar outcomes may emerge from local, incremental learning processes.",
